  "text": "CasePath\nEvidence into action\nRead-only\nCases\nDemonstration\nKnowledge\nNext case Heating resets and an uncertain onset date is unavailable: The recorded replay head changed. Reopen to verify its newest history. The last verified case remains visible.\n\nCases / Synthetic claim / Recorded investigation\n\nRepeated heating failure and reported repair calls\n\nHistorical synthetic recording · as of 2025-02-21 · rules-based\n\nAssessment complete. Assessment only; no external action taken.\n\nPlay\nChoose case\nHistory\nProcess\nDocuments\nKnowledge\nSources\n\nThe fictional source packet supports defect removal and proportional reduction eligibility from documented landlord knowledge until remedy. The reduction amount, repair itself and any award remain undetermined.\n\nLegal basis · CO 259 · CO 259a · CO 259d · Recorded 2024-01-01 comparison\n\nFrom the sources\n02-heating-service-observation.txt\n↗\nOn 2025-02-21 at07:30, a calibrated digital instrument (fictional calibration check2024-12-15, uncertainty±0.2C) measured the living room at15.8C after overnight normal operation. Main living rooms stayed15.5–16.3C in the seven-day logger record. Resets restore heat briefly; the pump cuts out repeatedly. The fixed circulation pump has an internal bearing/control failure; it is part of landlord-maintained equipment, outside ordinary small tenant maintenance. Normal ventilation and unobstructed radiators were observed; no tenant alteration or misuse explains the failure.\nWhat this shows\n\nThe dated calibrated observation identifies the fixed-pump fault and its causal limits.\n\nEstablished\n\nDefects and repairs\n\nAdded for reuse · Version 1\n\nOpen procedure\n\nAdded landlord knowledge and continuing repair status requirements: recipient, reported defect, first knowledge date, repair status.\n\nAdded dated technical defect observation requirements: location, observation date, observed fault, causal limits.\n\nAdded relevant tenancy terms requirements: contracting parties, property, tenancy terms.\n\nOpen larger process\n✓\nCapture the reported defect\n✓\nEstablish relevant tenancy terms\n✓\nEstablish landlord knowledge\n✓\nAssess supported cause\n✓\nAssess objective defect evidence\nCompleted\n✓\nRecord repair and rent reduction eligibility\nDocument requirements\nRelevant tenancy terms\nEstablished\nSupplied evidence is sufficient. ✓\nEstablish relevant tenancy terms\nSource evidence · 01-customer-and-tenancy-clarification.txt\nLandlord knowledge and continuing repair status\nEstablished\nSupplied evidence is sufficient. ✓\nEstablish landlord knowledge\nSource evidence · 03-landlord-knowledge-and-repair-status.txt\nDated technical defect observation\nEstablished\nSupplied evidence is sufficient. ✓\nAssess objective defect evidence\nSource evidence · 02-heating-service-observation.txt\nAll recorded requirements",
