uipment, outside ordinary small tenant maintenance. Normal ventilation and unobstructed radiators were observed; no tenant alteration or misuse explains the failure.&quot;,&quot;sha256&quot;:&quot;ad1d46adcf2f5cff2e4be0b9db7bbc5fdd07577badbea246604470f38bcf9fa3&quot;,&quot;start_char&quot;:734,&quot;text_sha256&quot;:&quot;ad1d46adcf2f5cff2e4be0b9db7bbc5fdd07577badbea246604470f38bcf9fa3&quot;}\" data-au-source-origin=\"path:dh_evidence:fact:objective_defect_observation\"><span class=\"au-evidence-source-label\">02-heating-service-observation.txt<span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></span><q>On 2025-02-21 at07:30, a calibrated digital instrument (fictional calibration check2024-12-15, uncertainty±0.2C) measured the living room at15.8C after overnight normal operation. Main living rooms stayed15.5–16.3C in the seven-day logger record. Resets restore heat briefly; the pump cuts out repeatedly. The fixed circulation pump has an internal bearing/control failure; it is part of landlord-maintained equipment, outside ordinary small tenant maintenance. Normal ventilation and unobstructed radiators were observed; no tenant alteration or misuse explains the failure.</q></button></section><section class=\"au-reading-fact\" data-au-fact=\"fact:objective_defect_observation\"><h3 class=\"au-reading-label\">What this shows</h3><p class=\"au-fact-summary\">The dated calibrated observation identifies the fixed-pump fault and its causal limits.</p><p class=\"au-fact-state\">Established</p></section></div></div><section class=\"au-forming-process au-evidence-process\" aria-label=\"Complete process\"><div class=\"au-forming-publication-focus\" data-au-publication-focus=\"531ece50046c4c940e7f4d2249f50cb6af74927fa7c5417c9848c15409bb9cab\"><section class=\"au-forming-knowledge\" aria-label=\"Procedure use and additions\"><article class=\"au-knowledge-publication\" data-au-knowledge-publication=\"d8c5d9bde122f9ec081615e212af0ae2fb22e1fa5df08f39d9c28b491ac6b1eb\"><h3>Defects and repairs</h3><p